      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "7 crosses, 7 triangles"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "none of these are possible"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Look at the corners",
        "body": "At each corner of the cube three squares meet, one from each of three faces, and each pair of them shares an edge. So the three squares at a corner must show three different shapes: one cross, one triangle, one circle.\n\nEach of the 24 squares touches exactly one corner, and the cube has 8 corners, so there are exactly $8$ crosses, $8$ triangles and $8$ circles. None of the options (A) to (D) has this, so none is possible.\n\n**Answer: (E) none of these are possible**"
      }
